// examples/layout_window.ent without a window: a device that prints what
// would be drawn stands in for devices/window.c, which needs a display
// and raylib. What is drawn, in which order, clipped, shifted and shaded
// how; boxes on their way to another place, size, colour, corners and
// border (Transition, Enter, Leave, Gone), a box the program draws and a
// way of easing that is the program's (a proc and a fn as values),
// overlays on
// one another, what scrolls dragged and let go, and the inspector.
// RUN: sh %S/Inputs/headless.sh %t.dir
// RUN: %ent run -I %t.dir -I %S/../../examples %S/Inputs/layout_draw.ent \
// RUN:     2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// Under half of black, the window and the list; what is in the list
// within it, and not the third row, which is below its end.
// CHECK:      frame 1
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.50
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 0 0 300 200 00101010
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 10 10 100 180 00202020
// CHECK-NEXT: clip 10 10 100 180
// CHECK-NEXT: write 14 14 in 92 "row 0" 00ffffff
// CHECK-NEXT: write 14 124 in 92 "row 1" 00ffffff
// CHECK-NEXT: unclip
// The card is on its way up from 40 below, a fifth of the way (it says
// `always`: the window it is in is new too); its red comes on with it,
// on the black: more of both together than of either. The text in it
// goes with it, and does not come from above as it would in a card that
// was there before.
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 32
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 180000 0.53
// CHECK-NEXT: rounded 120 10 170 180 by 8 8 0 0 ff304050
// CHECK-NEXT: write 130 20 in 150 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// The edges after all the boxes, each as its box is drawn; and the lines
// between the rows of the list, in the middle of its gaps.
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 0
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.50
// CHECK-NEXT: edges 10 10 100 180 of 0 0 0 0 00404040
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 32
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 180000 0.53
// CHECK-NEXT: edges 120 10 170 180 of 1 1 3 1 ff3a7bd5
// CHECK-NEXT: clip 10 10 100 180
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 0
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.50
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 10 114 100 2 00404040
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 10 224 100 2 00404040
// CHECK-NEXT: unclip
// What floats, a layer above: with the box it floats over, its middle on
// that one's corner.
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 32
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 180000 0.53
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 277 17 6 6 00e05040
// And a box the program draws itself: its proc is called where the box
// comes, under what is laid on the window.
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 0
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.50
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 20 170 60 16 00123456
// CHECK-NEXT: label 22 172 "mark 7"
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.00
// (The pointer is where the card is, and does not find it: it is on its
// way.)
// With nothing left out for being out of sight, the third row too: it
// is drawn, and the list lets none of it show.
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 2
// CHECK:      write 14 234 in 92 "row 2" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      shift 0 24
// CHECK:      frame 3
// CHECK:      write 14 14 in 92 "row 0" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      shift 0 16
// The pointer went down on the list, and is 30 further up.
// CHECK:      frame 4
// CHECK:      write 14 -16 in 92 "row 0" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      shift 0 8
// Let go, the list goes on, and the third row shows; the card is where
// it is to be, under a quarter of red on half of black. It has a bar
// under its text now, which comes from 20 to the left: the card was
// there before it. In a way of the program's own, a fn that the bar's
// Transition names: not at all for half the time, and then all at once.
// CHECK:      frame 5
// CHECK:      write 14 -31 in 92 "row 0" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      write 14 189 in 92 "row 2" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      shade 660000 0.63
// CHECK-NEXT: rounded 120 10 170 180 by 8 8 0 0 00304050
// CHECK-NEXT: write 130 20 in 150 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK-NEXT: shift -20 0
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 130 68 150 20 00505050
// CHECK-NEXT: shift 0 0
// Slower and slower. The pointer is on the card, which is where it is to
// be.
// CHECK:      frame 6
// CHECK:      write 14 -41.5 in 92 "row 0" 00ffffff
// CHECK:      shift -20 0
// CHECK:      the pointer is on the card
// Its colour is to be another: a fifth of the way a frame. And the list
// is 40 narrower, so the card is to start 40 further left and be as
// much wider: it is 32 from there still, and 8 wider. What is in it is
// laid out for how wide it is right now: the text has 8 more, and what
// floats at the text's corner is 8 further right. Its first corner is to
// be 10 rounder, and the edge at its top 10 thicker and white: each a
// fifth of the way. The bar is as far from its place as the card: it is
// where it is to be in the card now.
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 7
// CHECK:      rect 10 10 60 180 00202020
// CHECK:      shift 32 0
// CHECK:      rounded 80 10 178 180 by 10 8 0 0 ff306650
// CHECK-NEXT: write 90 20 in 158 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 90 52 150 20 00505050
// CHECK:      edges 80 10 178 180 of 1 1 5 1 ff6195dd
// CHECK:      rect 245 17 6 6 00e05040
// CHECK:      frame 8
// CHECK:      shift 24 0
// CHECK:      rounded 80 10 186 180 by 12 8 0 0 ff308c50
// CHECK-NEXT: write 90 20 in 166 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK:      edges 80 10 186 180 of 1 1 7 1 ff89b0e6
// CHECK:      rect 253 17 6 6 00e05040
// It is to go: it takes no room in the window's row any more, and is
// apart where it was, drawn before the others there (so under them,
// where they come to be over it), under more and more of the colour it
// leaves into. It goes on getting wider and rounder as it did, and is as
// wide as it is to be half a second after it set out for that.
// CHECK:      frame 9
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 000000 0.50
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 0 0 300 200 00101010
// CHECK-NEXT: shift {{[0-9.]+}} 0
// CHECK-NEXT: shade 760202 0.70
// CHECK-NEXT: rounded 80 10 194 180 by 14 8 0 0 ff30a350
// CHECK-NEXT: write 90 20 in 174 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK:      rect 10 10 60 180 00202020
// The text in it goes its own way out with it, 30 down in half a
// second: its `Leave` says it follows. It is apart in the card from then
// on, as wide as it was, and the bar is where the text was.
// CHECK:      frame 10
// CHECK:      shift {{[0-9.]+}} 6
// CHECK-NEXT: write 90 20 in 174 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK:      rect 90 20 174 20 00505050
// CHECK:      frame 11
// CHECK:      rounded 80 10 210 180 by 18 8 0 0 ff30d150
// CHECK-NEXT: shift {{[0-9.]+}} 12
// CHECK-NEXT: write 90 20 in 174 "a text that goes on in the next line" 00a0b0c0
// CHECK:      edges 80 10 210 180 of 1 1 13 1 00ffffff
// CHECK:      frame 13
// CHECK:      shade 101010 1.00
// CHECK-NEXT: rounded 80 10 210 180 by 18 8 0 0 0030ff50
// And is gone, with the text and the bar in it and what floated over
// that.
// CHECK:      frame 14
// CHECK-NOT:  rounded
// CHECK-NOT:  a text that goes on
// CHECK-NOT:  505050
// CHECK-NOT:  rect 277 17 6 6
// CHECK:      frame 15
// The inspector, at the right of the window: the boxes line by line, each
// further in than the box it is in, what floats under the box it floats
// over (after the boxes in that one), and all about the one the pointer
// is on, which is marked in the window.
// CHECK:      rect 380 0 320 260 f0141a20
// CHECK:      label 406 11 "row 300 x 200"
// CHECK:      label 418 29 "clip 60 x 180"
// CHECK:      label 430 47 "text 60 x 100"
// CHECK:      label 430 65 "text 60 x 100"
// CHECK:      label 430 83 "text 60 x 100"
// CHECK:      label 418 101 "float 60 x 16"
// CHECK:      clip 0 0 380 260
// CHECK:      edges 10 {{[0-9.]+}} 60 100 of 2 2 2 2 00ffe040
// CHECK:      label 390 138 "line 4, layer 0, 2 deep"
// CHECK:      label 390 174 "width grow, height fixed"
// CHECK:      label 390 192 "padding 4 4 4 4, gap 0"
// CHECK:      label 390 228 "row 1"
